From 70bba49d773d694c9fe5fc3769919e937b1a480a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:40:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] [Pascal] Host-mapped two-rank all-reduce; disable the IPC
 custom all-reduce

The IPC custom all-reduce spin-waits on peer memory and hangs on Pascal PCIe
cards behind different CPU sockets. PascalHostAllreduce exchanges through
mapped pinned host memory in one graph-capturable kernel: 19.5 vs 33.5 us per
decode-sized all-reduce against NCCL. VLLM_PASCAL_HOST_ALLREDUCE=0 disables it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
